+// The number of src1 rows that the same-shape path moves for a block of src0 rows. With ne11 == 1,
+// all rows of a block use the same src1 row. The split flags keep a block in one plane of dim 2 when
+// ne12 > 1, and in one plane of dim 3 when ne13 > 1. Thus the block moves one src1 row. One src1 row
+// for each src0 row at the stride nb11 reads the rows of the next planes, or past the end of src1.
+static inline uint32_t binary_src1_block_rows(uint32_t ne11, uint32_t block_rows) {
+    return ne11 == 1 ? 1 : block_rows;
+}
